**app/poltergeist_app/test/ui/demo/sftp_demo_view_test.dart:1 - Entire SFTP demo widget test suite deleted with no replacement visible in this section**
**Problem:** This section removes the full ~1865-line test suite for the SFTP demo view. The deleted suite encodes a substantial amount of hard-won behavioral coverage, including:
- Debug gating (`debugDemoEnabled: false` hides the command, app asserts no factory when gated off)
- Session lifecycle teardown (route close → prompts closed, browse channel `closeCalls == 1`, engine `shutdownCalls == 1`)
- System-back dismissing an open prompt on the nested navigator before the route pops
- The double-tap/in-flight guard preventing two engine spawns
- Host-key prompt flows (first use, changed key, declined changed key → `blocked` vs `disconnected` status)
- Probe ordering regression (#55: subscribe to `probeStatuses` before sending probe commands — `probeCommandsSawListener`)
- Open re-entrancy gating (`openGate`) and stale disconnect cleanup ordering (`disconnectGate`)
- Unhandled-message loud failure in `scriptedDemoEngineMain` when the protocol grows a new dependency
None of this is re-added within this chunk, so it is impossible to tell from this section whether the coverage was migrated or silently dropped.
**Impact:** If these cases were not carried over to new files (e.g., a split of the monolithic test into per-feature files), regressions in `SftpDemoController`/`SftpDemoView` and the engine port semantics they pin down — several of which guard specific past bugs like the #55 ordering rule — would ship undetected. Even if the move is intentional, an unverified bulk deletion of regression tests is the single highest-risk change in a PR.
**Suggested fix:**
```diff
- test/ui/demo/sftp_demo_view_test.dart deleted in full (1865 lines)
+ Verify every deleted group/case has an equivalent in the new split test
+ files before merging. Any dropped case must be restored in the closest
+ new file rather than re-adding this monolith.
```
**Prompt for AI Agents:**
```
1. Run `git show HEAD:app/poltergeist_app/test/ui/demo/sftp_demo_view_test.dart` and enumerate every testWidgets case and group name.
2. Grep the new test/ tree for equivalent coverage of each: (a) debug gating + no-factory assertion, (b) command opens demo + teardown shutdown/channel-close counts, (c) back dismisses prompt before route pop, (d) narrow-window toolbar, (e) double-tap single spawn, (f) hostKeyFirstUse/hostKeyChanged accept+decline flows including blocked-vs-disconnected status, (g) probe snapshot-before-ack and listener-before-command ordering, (h) openGate re-entrancy, (i) disconnectGate stale-cleanup ordering, (j) scriptedDemoEngineMain unhandled-message loud failure.
3. For any deleted case with no matching new test, add it to the most appropriate new test file using the existing fakes in that file.
4. If the migration is complete, note the mapping in the PR description so reviewers can confirm no coverage was lost.
```

**app/poltergeist_app/test/ui/panes/pane_view_test.dart:616 - Semantics finder throws without `ensureSemantics()`**
**Problem:** `find.bySemanticsLabel` requires the semantics pipeline to be enabled, which is off by default in widget tests. Without a `tester.ensureSemantics()` handle, the finder throws (`Semantics are not enabled. Make sure to call WidgetTester.ensureSemantics() ...`) before any label matching happens. Nothing else in this test (or `pumpShell`) enables semantics.
**Impact:** This test deterministically fails in CI with a framework error rather than actually verifying the row's semantic label, so the a11y contract it claims to lock down is not tested at all.
**Suggested fix:**
```diff
   testWidgets('rows announce name, size, and date to semantics', (
     tester,
   ) async {
-    localChannelWithEntries();
+    final handle = tester.ensureSemantics();
+    addTearDown(handle.dispose);
+
+    localChannelWithEntries();
     await left.openLocalHome();
     await pumpShell(tester);
```
**Prompt for AI Agents:**
```
Run: flutter test test/ui/panes/pane_view_test.dart --plain-name "rows announce name, size, and date to semantics"
Confirm it fails with a "Semantics are not enabled" error. Insert `final handle = tester.ensureSemantics();` followed by `addTearDown(handle.dispose);` as the first statements of the test body, then re-run until the test passes for the right reason (one matched Semantics node).
```
